ATTRIBUTION AND PROVENANCE
--------------------------
This corpus is DERIVED FROM BANKING77:

    Casanueva, I., Temcinas, T., Gerz, D., Henderson, M., and Vulic, I. (2020).
    Efficient Intent Detection with Dual Sentence Encoders.
    Proceedings of the 2nd Workshop on Natural Language Processing for
    Conversational AI, pages 38-45.
    https://huggingface.co/datasets/PolyAI/banking77

BANKING77 is itself released under CC BY 4.0. This corpus is redistributed under
the same licence, as that licence requires.

WHAT IS INHERITED AND WHAT IS NEW
---------------------------------
Inherited from BANKING77:
  - the English ticket text
  - the 77-way intent taxonomy and its human gold labels

Added by this work:
  - Sinhala, Tamil and romanized (Singlish / Tanglish) renderings of each ticket
  - sentiment and priority labels, which are LLM-generated from a documented
    prompt pipeline and are NOT human gold; see paper/drafts/data_statement.md
  - the frozen train/dev/test split, drawn on ticket id so that the five renderings
    of one ticket never straddle the split

CITING THIS CORPUS
------------------
Citing BANKING77 alone is not sufficient attribution. Of 65,385 rows, 52,308 (80%)
carry text this project produced, and two of the three label columns are this
project's. See CITATION.cff at the repository root for BibTeX, or the dataset card
at https://huggingface.co/datasets/Swift-Support/swift-support-tickets-1.0

Users redistributing this corpus must carry both attributions.
